Lüneburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Augustus the Younger was Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg who ruled the Principality of Wolfenbüttel from 1635 until his death in 1666.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/augustus-duke-of-saxe-weissenfels"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/augustus-duke-of-saxe-weissenfels.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Augustus, Duke of Saxe-Weissenfels</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Augustus was a son of Elector John George I of Saxony and administrator of the Archbishopric of Magdeburg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/auisle"><span class="enc-name">Auisle</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Auisle was a Viking leader in Ireland in the 860s, who with Amlaíb (Olaf) ruled the Norse of Dublin and is described in Irish sources as Amlaíb's brother.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/auktume"><span class="enc-name">Auktume</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Auktume was a leader of the Pogesanians, one of the Old Prussian peoples, during the Great Prussian Uprising against the Teutonic Order that began in 1260.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aukus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aukus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">AUKUS</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">AUKUS is a security partnership between Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States announced in September 2021.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/auld-alliance"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/auld-alliance.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Auld Alliance</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Auld Alliance was the alliance between Scotland and France against England, first sealed by a treaty of 1295 between John Balliol and Philip IV and renewed by most…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/auld-lang-syne"><span class="enc-name">Auld Lang Syne</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">&quot;Auld Lang Syne&quot; is a poem in Scots that Robert Burns wrote in 1788 on the basis of an older Scottish folk song.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulerci"><span class="enc-name">Aulerci</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aulerci were a group of related Gallic peoples in north-western Gaul, named by Julius Caesar.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulic-council"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aulic-council.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aulic Council</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aulic Council, or Reichshofrat, was one of the two supreme courts of the Holy Roman Empire, alongside the Imperial Chamber Court.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulic-war-council"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aulic-war-council.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aulic War Council</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aulic War Council, or Hofkriegsrat, was the central military administration of the Habsburg Monarchy, established in Vienna in 1556.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulikara-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Aulikara dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aulikara dynasty ruled the region of Dashapura, modern Mandsaur in western Malwa, in the fifth and sixth centuries CE, at first as subordinates of the Gupta Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-cornelius-cossus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aulus-cornelius-cossus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Cornelius Cossus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Cornelius Cossus was a Roman commander of the 5th century BCE who killed Lars Tolumnius, king of Veii, in single combat during the war over Fidenae.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-gabinius"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Gabinius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Gabinius was a Roman politician and general.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-plautius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aulus-plautius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Plautius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Plautius was a Roman senator and general who commanded the invasion of Britain ordered by the emperor Claudius in 43 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-postumius-albinus"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Postumius Albinus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Postumius Albinus was a Roman commander in the Jugurthine War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-terentius-varro-murena"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Terentius Varro Murena</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Terentius Varro Murena was a Roman general in the early reign of Augustus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-vibenna"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aulus-vibenna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Vibenna</span><span class="enc-type">Person</s